Subject: [PATCH] yazi-fm: skip tikv-jemallocator on target_env="ohos"

tikv-jemalloc-sys 0.6.1 bundles a config.sub that does not recognise
`aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos`, so its build.rs autoconf step fails with
`Invalid configuration 'aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos': OS 'ohos' not
recognized`.

yazi-fm only adds the dependency for non-macOS / non-Windows builds and
declares the global allocator behind the same cfg gate, so we extend
both gates to also exclude `target_env = "ohos"`. The system allocator
is used on OHOS until either tikv-jemalloc-sys ships a newer config.sub
or yazi bumps past 0.6.1.

---
 yazi-fm/Cargo.toml  | 2 +-
 yazi-fm/src/main.rs | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/yazi-fm/Cargo.toml b/yazi-fm/Cargo.toml
--- a/yazi-fm/Cargo.toml
+++ b/yazi-fm/Cargo.toml
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@ libc              = { workspace = true }
 [target.'cfg(target_os = "macos")'.dependencies]
 crossterm = { workspace = true, features = [ "use-dev-tty", "libc" ] }

-[target.'cfg(all(not(target_os = "macos"), not(target_os = "windows")))'.dependencies]
+[target.'cfg(all(not(target_os = "macos"), not(target_os = "windows"), not(target_env = "ohos")))'.dependencies]
 tikv-jemallocator = "0.6.1"

 [[bin]]
diff --git a/yazi-fm/src/main.rs b/yazi-fm/src/main.rs
--- a/yazi-fm/src/main.rs
+++ b/yazi-fm/src/main.rs
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-#[cfg(all(not(target_os = "macos"), not(target_os = "windows")))]
+#[cfg(all(not(target_os = "macos"), not(target_os = "windows"), not(target_env = "ohos")))]
 #[global_allocator]
 static GLOBAL: tikv_jemallocator::Jemalloc = tikv_jemallocator::Jemalloc;

